First, let's find an expression for $H'(x)$ in terms of $g'$ and $h'$:

$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}H'(x)
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}H(x)&&\gray{\text{Equivalent notation}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[4g(x)+5h(x)-7]&&\gray{\text{Substitute the expression for }H(x)}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{d}{dx}[4g(x)]+\dfrac{d}{dx}[5h(x)]-\dfrac{d}{dx}(7)&&\gray{\text{Sum and difference rules}}
\\\\
&=4g'(x)+5h'(x)-0&&\gray{\text{Constant and constant multiple rules}}
\end{align}$

So we found that $H'(x)=4g'(x)+5h'(x)$.
